      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Background of the Mauryan Empire"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Mauryan Empire was established by Chandragupta Maurya after defeating the Nanda dynasty with Chanakya's guidance.",
        "Bindusara expanded the empire further south and maintained diplomatic ties with Hellenistic rulers.",
        "Ashoka embraced non-violence and propagated Dhamma across Asia following the devastating Kalinga War.",
        "Mauryan administration was highly centralized and documented in detail in Kautilya's Arthashastra and Megasthenes' Indica.",
        "Mauryan art features distinct polished monolithic pillars, rock edicts, and stupas like the Sanchi Stupa."
      ],
      "id": "340p6fw"
    },
